# ...but the scripts directories hold maintained tooling, not throwaways. Those
# patterns are unanchored, so `check_*.py` silently swallowed
# scripts/check_schema_drift.py (task H1.11). Negations must follow the patterns
# they override — last match wins.
#
# H5.7: the negation covered backend/scripts/ only, so the SAME trap caught
# scripts/check_slo.py at the root. Both are un-ignored now.
!backend/scripts/**
!scripts/**
# ...and the same trap pointing the other way: `**` un-ignores EVERYTHING under
# those directories, including the caches the global `__pycache__/` rule at the
# top was already handling. Found 2026-08-25, when backend/scripts/__pycache__/
# showed up as untracked next to the H3.4 gates. Same shape as the
# backend/tests/ block below, which got this right first.
backend/scripts/**/__pycache__/
backend/scripts/**/*.py[cod]
scripts/**/__pycache__/
scripts/**/*.py[cod]

# Backend test suite is VERSIONED (undo gates, regressions) — the temp-script
# `test_*.py` rules above must never swallow it. Only caches stay ignored.
# The application package is SOURCE. The throwaway-script patterns above are
# unanchored, so `export_*.py` silently took app/services/export_cleanup.py —
# a real 7.8KB module the startup path imports. It has never been in the
# repository, so every deploy ran without it and swallowed the ImportError as
# "Startup export cleanup failed (non-critical)": temp exports were never
# cleaned up anywhere but this machine. Caches under app/uploads/ stay ignored.
!backend/app/**
backend/app/uploads/
backend/app/**/__pycache__/
backend/app/**/*.py[cod]

!backend/tests/**
backend/tests/**/__pycache__/
backend/tests/**/*.py[cod]
backend/tests/**/.pytest_cache/

